			"71": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 1: HEIGHT AND WIDTH\n\nIn this example we use the Patch Info node to get the aspect ratio of the patch.\nThis is sent to to the widht inlet of the Rectangle to make sure the Rectangle is the correct width for the texture we give it in the Mesh 2D node.\nWe are also sending a Sine, running from-1 to 1, to the Rectangle's height inlet.\nNote that when the height is negative, the output is flipped upside down.\nThe Rectangle is sent to the Mesh 2D node to construct a mesh 2d type.\nNext we patch it to the Render 2D node to render it to a texture."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 488.41900634765625,
					"width": 1105.744140625,
					"x": -398.46575927734375,
					"y": 14.8494110107421875
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "fff26eb5",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
			"72": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 2: UV\n\nIn this example we've changed  the UV values from 0,0,1,1 to 0,0,18,18.\nThis causes the texture to repeat itself, giving us a whole lot of copies!\nThis method can be used to creat incredibly lightweight repeating effects. "
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 487.266937255859375,
					"width": 842.2432861328125,
					"x": 748.041259765625,
					"y": 16.80733489990234375
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffae7bff",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
			"73": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 3: POLYGON MADNESS\n\nIn this final example we're demonstating the power of meshes.\nIn the final result we've got 100 polyons on the screen.\nDoing this with shapes would grind you GPU to a halt.\n\nInstead, we are generating a single polygon using Perlin Generator, Polygon and Edge.\nNext, we turn the shape into materials using the Texture Material.\nColor is added by joining 3 colors together and we end up with a collection of 2 texture materials (hover over the oulet of the node to see that it is a collection).\n\nAt the top  we are creating a collection of 10 Rectangles by sending a Linear collection into the widht and height inlets. \nThis gives us squares in different sizes.\n\nThe Random node is used to generate a collection of 100 Float2 values that are used to position the meshes.\nThe Linear node is used to rotate the meshes "
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 1190.670654296875,
					"width": 1989.5855712890625,
					"x": -400.1951904296875,
					"y": 550.7547607421875
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffe53357",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
			"75": {
				"attributes": {
					"flow": {
						"type": "flow",
						"value": "signal"
