			"80": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "RECTANGLE\n\nThe Rectangle node constructs a rectangular geometry.\nThe width and height van be adjusted to your needs.\nThe UV parameters of the node are hidden by default but can be accessed through by right clicking the node and navigating to View.\n\nThe UV inlet takes a Box2D type which can be constructed with the Box2D node or Bounding Box node.\n\nBelow you can find three examples that use the Rectangle node and all its parameters."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 238.3932037353515625,
					"width": 489.463531494140625,
